# How to cite this repository, in Citation File Format 1.2.0. GitHub reads this file for its
# "Cite this repository" box. Zenodo does not: it reads .zenodo.json, so the two files must say
# the same, and tests/test_release_metadata.py checks that they do.
# The version, the release date and the DOI are written in on the day of a release; see the
# checklist in planning/specs/release.md.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "PyNMDF: Python for Network Minimum Demand Forecasting"
abstract: >-
  PyNMDF is the reproducible analysis code behind research on forecasting minimum demand in
  distribution networks as rooftop photovoltaic (PV) capacity grows. It holds one shared
  package and one folder per publication. Every input is public.
